2	/**
3	 * readme-map.mjs — gate `readme-map` (contract `kumitate-readme-map-v2`, round 58;
4	 * amends v1 of round 57 by the routed defect R57-V3 repair).
5	 *
6	 * The corpus coverage-map bimap gate. `proxy-check`'s C2 term compares only the
7	 * *counts* of `corpus/README.md` map rows against corpus `*.md` files — so a
8	 * file landing without a row surfaces one count drift, named and repaired by
9	 * hand (r52, r55, r56 verifier spotchecks; routed defect R56-V3). This gate
10	 * makes the mapping itself the contract: every `*.md` under
11	 * `corpus/knowledge` + `corpus/lessons` must carry exactly one README row
12	 * `| `path` |`, every such row must name an existing file, and every live
13	 * file must be pinned in the `covered` set.
14	 *
15	 *   node scripts/readme-map.mjs [--registry <path>] [--readme <path>]
16	 *                               [--corpus <dir>] ...
17	 *   node scripts/readme-map.mjs --selftest
18	 *
19	 * Verdicts (one line on stdout, after optional per-item notes):
20	 *   README_MAP: CLEAN files=<n> rows=<n> covered=<n>   exit 0
21	 *   README_MAP: DRIFT files=<n> rows=<n> covered=<m> bad=<k> first=<item>   exit 1
22	 *   README_MAP: FAIL-CLOSED reason=<why>                exit 2 (could not evaluate)
23	 *   README_MAP: USAGE ...                               exit 64
24	 *
25	 * Registry (default `.ufo/pins/readme-map.json`, lane-root-relative):
26	 *   { "version": 2, "covered": ["knowledge/x.md", "lessons/y.md", ...] }
27	 *
28	 * v2 (R57-V3): `covered` members are scored by NAME only no longer. Every
29	 * pinned member is lstat'd and must be a regular file: a member naming a
30	 * directory or other non-file is DRIFT `covered-not-file:<path>`; a member
31	 * whose lstat succeeds but whose target is gone — a dangling symlink — is
32	 * DRIFT `stale-covered:<path>` (a symlink whose target exists is likewise
33	 * not a regular file: `covered-not-file`). The registry moves to
34	 * `version: 2` (format unchanged — the version number now attests the
35	 * lstat semantics); a version 1 registry is FAIL-CLOSED.
36	 *
37	 * `covered` is the pinned set of corpus paths (`knowledge/` or `lessons/`
38	 * relpath, unique) that must BOTH exist AND keep a README row — the ratchet:
39	 * a corpus file can never lose its row or disappear silently again.
40	 *
41	 * Row rule: a coverage-map row is a table line whose FIRST cell is a single
42	 * backticked `knowledge/…` or `lessons/…` path — `| `knowledge/x.md` | …`.
43	 * Rows of any other shape in the README are ignored; a row whose first cell
44	 * *looks* corpus-bound (starts `knowledge/` or `lessons/` but is not a clean
45	 * backticked path) is DRIFT `format-unmapped`, never silently dropped.
46	 *
47	 * Findings:
48	 *   - DRIFT `uncovered:<path>` — a live `*.md` with no row.
49	 *   - DRIFT `orphan-row:<path>` — a row naming a path with no file.
50	 *   - DRIFT `duplicate-row:<path>` — two or more rows for one path.
51	 *   - DRIFT `format-unmapped:<cell>` — a corpus-shaped first cell that does
52	 *     not parse as a clean `| `path` |` row.
53	 *   - DRIFT `stale-covered:<path>` — a `covered` entry whose file is gone
54	 *     (including a dangling symlink: the name resolves, the target does not).
55	 *   - DRIFT `covered-not-file:<path>` — a `covered` entry whose lstat is not
56	 *     a regular file (a directory, a symlink to anything, a fifo).
57	 *   - DRIFT `unpinned:<path>` — a live file absent from `covered` (the pin
58	 *     grows by append when a file lands; the registry is never rewritten).
59	 *   - FAIL-CLOSED (exit 2, never a score): registry unreadable / not JSON /
60	 *     version ≠ 2 / `covered` not an array / a covered entry malformed,
61	 *     duplicated or outside `knowledge|lessons/`; README unreadable; a corpus
62	 *     directory missing; zero `*.md` files across the corpus dirs.
63	 *
64	 * The gate never writes. It reads the registry, the README and the corpus
65	 * directories only.
66	 *
67	 * Selftest: hermetic fixtures under mkdtemp, sixteen cases, one red-before
68	 * per rule; the final line reads `README_MAP_SELFTEST: PASS (16/16)` +
69	 * `VERDICT: PASS`, exit 0.
70	 *
71	 * Exit map: 0 clean · 1 a real defect (drift) · 2 fail-closed · 64 usage.
72	 * Owner: kumitate L1. Row: SKILL.md §Gate registry (`readme-map`, gate);
73	 * pin: SCORECARD.md `kumitate-gate-pins-v1` (`pin.readme-map`).
74	 */
